    "parsing_res_list": [
      {
        "block_label": "header",
        "block_content": "HIPPODROME CASINO LIMITED ",
        "block_bbox": [
          259,
          292,
          1114,
          341
        ],
        "block_id": 0,
        "block_order": 1
      },
      {
        "block_label": "paragraph_title",
        "block_content": "DIRECTORS'REPORT (CONTINUED)FOR THE YEAR ENDED 31 DECEMBER 2025",
        "block_bbox": [
          256,
          419,
          1273,
          546
        ],
        "block_id": 1,
        "block_order": 2
      },
      {
        "block_label": "paragraph_title",
        "block_content": "Employee involvement ",
        "block_bbox": [
          257,
          660,
          683,
          697
        ],
        "block_id": 2,
        "block_order": 3
      },
      {
        "block_label": "text",
        "block_content": "The Company's policy is to consult and discuss with employees, staff councils and at meetings, matters likely to affect employees' interests.\n",
        "block_bbox": [
          255,
          709,
          2200,
          791
        ],
        "block_id": 3,
        "block_order": 4
      },
      {
        "block_label": "text",
        "block_content": "Information of matters of concern to employees is given through information bulletins and reports which seek to achieve a common awareness.\n",
        "block_bbox": [
          254,
          838,
          2199,
          919
        ],
        "block_id": 4,
        "block_order": 5
      },
      {
        "block_label": "text",
        "block_content": "The Company is committed to employee consultation at all levels and encourages their involvement in the development of the Company's business. The Company operates an in-house newsletter to underpin the employee communications programme.\n",
        "block_bbox": [
          254,
          968,
          2199,
          1091
        ],
        "block_id": 5,
        "block_order": 6
      },
      {
        "block_label": "paragraph_title",
        "block_content": "Auditor ",
        "block_bbox": [
          259,
          1153,
          404,
          1186
        ],
        "block_id": 6,
        "block_order": 7
      },
      {
        "block_label": "text",
        "block_content": "The auditor, RSM UK Audit LLP, is deemed to be reappointed under section 487(2) of the Companies Act 2006",
        "block_bbox": [
          258,
          1200,
          2120,
          1240
        ],
        "block_id": 7,
        "block_order": 8
      },
      {
        "block_label": "paragraph_title",
        "block_content": "Statement of disclosure to auditor ",
        "block_bbox": [
          257,
          1300,
          884,
          1334
        ],
        "block_id": 8,
        "block_order": 9
      },
      {
        "block_label": "text",
        "block_content": "So far as each person who was a director at the date of approving this report is aware, there is no relevant audit information of which the Company's auditor is unaware. Additionally, each director has taken al the necessary steps that they ought to have taken as a director in order to make themselves aware of all relevant audit information and to establish that the Company's auditor is aware of that information.\n",
        "block_bbox": [
          254,
          1349,
          2199,
          1515
        ],
        "block_id": 9,
        "block_order": 10
      },
      {
        "block_label": "paragraph_title",
        "block_content": "Going concern ",
        "block_bbox": [
          258,
          1578,
          536,
          1612
        ],
        "block_id": 10,
        "block_order": 11
      },
      {
        "block_label": "text",
        "block_content": "The directors have prepared the financial statements on a going concern basis. In assessing the going concern position of the Company, the directors have considered the ongoing political and economic situations and their impact on the cash flow and liquidity of the Company over the next 12 months, and the corresponding impact on the covenants associated with our financing arrangements \n",
        "block_bbox": [
          255,
          1626,
          2200,
          1791
        ],
        "block_id": 11,
        "block_order": 12
      },
      {
        "block_label": "text",
        "block_content": "As at the balance sheet date the Company had cash reserves of £24,768,430 (2024: £30,767,822). The business is fully open, trading profitably and generating cash. The Company is reporting net current assets of £32,213,462(2024: £27,430,986) and has produced financial and cash flow forecasts sufficient to demonstrate the business will continue to trade profitably and meet all liabilities as they fall due.\n",
        "block_bbox": [
          254,
          1839,
          2200,
          2007
        ],
        "block_id": 12,
        "block_order": 13
      },
      {
        "block_label": "text",
        "block_content": "Included within the Company's net current assets is a debtor balance due from a group undertaking of £34,224,002(2024: £20,971,472). The balance is unsecured, interest free and repayable on demand, however the directors have confirmed that repayment is not expected to be demanded within the next 12 months. Having considered the recoverability of this balance, and supported by the profitable trading performance and cash reserves of the wider group, the directors are satisfied the balance is fully recoverable and does not present a risk to the Company's going concern position.\n",
        "block_bbox": [
          253,
          2055,
          2200,
          2310
        ],
        "block_id": 13,
        "block_order": 14
      },
      {
        "block_label": "text",
        "block_content": "Therefore the directors continue to adopt the going concern basis of accounting for the next 12 months in preparing the financial statements.\n",
        "block_bbox": [
          256,
          2357,
          2199,
          2434
        ],
        "block_id": 14,
        "block_order": 15
      },
      {
        "block_label": "paragraph_title",
        "block_content": "Matters of strategic importance ",
        "block_bbox": [
          258,
          2487,
          834,
          2521
        ],
        "block_id": 15,
        "block_order": 16
      },
      {
        "block_label": "text",
        "block_content": "The Company has chosen in accordance with Companies Act 2006, s. 414C(11) to set out in the Company's strategic report information required by Large and Medium-sized Companies and Groups (Accounts and Reports)Regulations 20o8, Sch. 7 to be contained in the directors' report. It has done so in respect of principal risks and uncertainties and future developments.\n",
        "block_bbox": [
          255,
          2528,
          2199,
          2694
        ],
        "block_id": 16,
        "block_order": 17
      },
      {
        "block_label": "paragraph_title",
        "block_content": "Streamlined Energy and Carbon Reporting ",
        "block_bbox": [
          258,
          2756,
          1035,
          2793
        ],
        "block_id": 17,
        "block_order": 18
      },
      {
        "block_label": "text",
        "block_content": "Hippodrome Casino Limited has taken exemption from the reporting requirements of SECR as this information is  included in the consolidated financial statements of Hippodrome Holdings Limited, the ultimate holding company.",
        "block_bbox": [
          256,
          2805,
          2198,
          2887
        ],
        "block_id": 18,
        "block_order": 19
      },
      {
        "block_label": "number",
        "block_content": "-12",
        "block_bbox": [
          1193,
          3316,
          1277,
          3346
        ],
        "block_id": 19,
        "block_order": 20
      }
    ],
